{{ToonInfo|type=Single|Toon=Rodger|extra=Magnifying Glass|Date=June 14, 2024|Pronoun=He}}

==Appearance==
Rodger is a brown magnifying glass with a single eye resting in the middle of his lens. His eye is perpetually squinted from above (perhaps in exhaustion, disdain, or focus). He has no visible mouth, but he is still able to speak. His handle has a light purple-ish blue band that goes around it. He wears a gray, almost-black tuxedo jacket with dark blue lapels and cuffs, as well as a white undershirt, and a frilly jabot that is the same color as the band around his handle. He also seems to have no noticeable trousers at the bottom.

In his full icon, he carries a brown suitcase with him.

==Personality==
Rodger is a clever and logical [[Toon]]. He formally carries himself and is generally polite and well-spoken. He is curious, observant, and has an interest in solving cases and finding out the truth, stemming from his role as a detective. This interest leads to him often interrogating and conducting interviews with the other Toons, resulting in him coming off as nosy or even pushy at times. Such cases can be seen in his interactions with {{CI|Astro|name=true}} and {{CI|Sprout|name=true}}, saying, "It may be safer, but uncovering truths is more rewarding!" and, "How about later? I could ask you after this!" even after being turned down.

Despite Rodger's pushiness and dedication to his work, he is by no means aloof and is actually quite caring towards his peers. In his dialogues, Rodger frequently compliments {{CI|Brightney|name=true}}, obtains help from her with his work, and looks out for her; much like she does for him. Additionally, he inquires about the well-being of other toons, and in one instance, even offers advice for calming down {{CI|Boxten|name=true}}. He has adopted some of {{CI|Glisten|name=true}}'s personality traits, according to one of his dialogues with {{CI|Eggson|name=true}}. Based on their interactions, it is clear that Rodger generally keeps things "behind closed doors", considering only a few toons like Brightney as trusted friends, and keeping  {{CI|Tisha|name=true}} strictly limited to his work.

In some official artwork and doodles (such as on the poster with him, Boxten, {{CI|Goob|name=true}}, {{CI|Razzle & Dazzle|name=true}}), Rodger seems to be photogenic, as his singular eye expresses happiness whenever he's looking at the camera.

==Mastery==
{{Mastery|Collect 1000% of [[Twisted Research]]|Encounter 100 Twisteds|Pick up 125 [[Research Capsules]]|Pick up 60 [[Items]]|Travel 75000 Meters|Use 60 Items}}

===Mastery Strategy===
{{MastComp|{{MastStrat|first|it's recommended to get encounters and [[Research Capsules]]. This is useful if you are finding a specific [[Twisted]], as you both get the Twisted's research and get extra research from other Twisteds. In fact, this could be done accidentally when doing other tasks.}}|{{MastStrat|second|Encounter Twisteds||Doing this task could also help speed up the completion of the first task.}}|{{MastStrat|third, fourth, and sixth|Collect and use|CapsAndUse|Doing the third task could also help speed up the completion of the first task.}}|{{MastStrat|fifth|Meters|2Star}}}}

==Requirement Strategies==
*For the first requirement, focus on picking up [[Research Capsules]] and extracting [[Machines]]. The Machine and Capsule count increases the further you descend, so you can earn more {{II|Ichor|name=true}}.
*For the second requirement, have a Distractor [[Toon]] bring any [[Twisted]] to the elevator to you so you can get aggro. It is recommended to get Research for {{Type|Common}} Twisteds, since they have a higher chance of appearing during the [[Floors]]. Another option is to get research is from the Twisted that is on the [[Daily Twisted Board]].

==Strategies==
Rodger's main purpose lies in collecting [[Research]] (and for lack of other proficiencies, {{TI|Ichor|name=true}}). He makes a good training character as using him is most beneficial for new players: his low Movement Speed helps players learn to regulate Stamina and his extra Research gain is most beneficial to those that don't have much. The rest of this section should be considered with the fact that he is ''more aptly-applied with the inexperienced'' in mind.

Rodger's main [[Stat]], which is his [[Extraction Speed]] (4{{Star}}), is above average and will help with completing [[Machines]] faster. The only downside is his low [[Movement Speed]], which means finding and using Speed [[Items]] will help with traversing around the [[Floor]] better (although you may wish to save them for emergencies). He is not very efficient as an extractor compared to other [[Toons]] with the inclination due to his propensity for seeking research and the hindrance of having difficulty traversing the map. 

Rodger's '''Detective''' Passive grants him double the Research percentages from collecting [[Research Capsules]] and encountering [[Twisteds]]. Normally, you would gain '''1%''' from Research Capsules and '''5%''' from encountering Twisteds, but with his Passive Ability, it's doubled to '''2%''' and '''10%'''. This makes Rodger useful for collecting Research much faster on a Twisted that isn't fully Researched yet. However, this effectively renders him ability-less (similarly to {{CI|Boxten|name=true}}). For that reason, if you have no motivation to collect Research (either because you have all of it or don't want it), Rodger probably isn't the best Toon for the job. If you do want Research, no other Toon surpasses him—so long as you have the teammates to back it up.

If one is using him primarily to search for Research, Movement Speed [[Trinkets]] may help to locate capsules before the Floor expires. Alternatively, Trinkets like Vee's Remote can be equipped to pass Floors faster to encounter more of your target Twisted. {{TI|Research Map|name=true}} can help you know where the Capsules are, so that you don't need to waste Stamina going to empty rooms.

