==Trivia==
*Despite popular belief caused by a rumor, Rodger does not lower {{Type|Main}} [[Twisted]] chances when in a round.
*Before [[Changelog|v0.4.1]], Rodger had a bug where picking up a [[Research Capsule]] as him would not give 2% if you hadn't encountered the [[Twisted]] before.
*You can look through before the glass in Rodger's head to see through [[Blackouts]] clearer like how you can with {{CI|Gigi|name=true}}'s plastic lid, as Roblox's rendering works poorly with fog seen through transparent objects.
*Assuming you enter a chase with a [[Twisted]] and collect their two [[Research Capsules]], it takes 8 encounters with a Twisted to get 100% [[Research]] on them, or technically 7.2 encounters, though there is no natural way to get a decimal amount of encounters.
*Rodger's eye and lens are layered on top of some effects ([[Stats]] boosts, username, [[Ichor]] from [[Machines]], etc.).
*Rodger's introduction card used to say that he was a spyglass. It was later corrected to say that he is a magnifying glass.
*Rodger's name is likely either a reference to {{wp|Roger Bacon}}, the inventor of the magnifying glass, or the saying "Roger that."
*Rodger's head is a circle, but the low-poly count on the 3D model turns it into an {{wp|octadecagon}}, which has 18 sides.
*Rodger's interaction with {{CI|Poppy|name=true}} reveals he is considering a monocle to add to his look.
*Rodger's tense dynamic with most of the [[Main Characters]] seems to stem from his interrogation attempts being considered pushy and obnoxious by them, but he gets along with [[Shelly]] just fine.
*Rodger is friends with {{CI|Toodles|name=true}}, {{CI|Brightney|name=true}}, and, {{CI|Glisten|name=true}} based on their interactions.
**Contrary to popular belief, Rodger is not Toodles' father. However, he still seems to go along with her, making sure to look after and protect her, and be someone to look up to.
**Rodger and Brightney have a mutual respect for each other, with Rodger often complimenting the latter's intelligence. Additionally, Brightney has helped Rodger with his cases and continues to offer assistance, showing a deep level of trust as Rodger's investigations are often confidential.
**Glisten often vents to Rodger and they're shown to be close enough to engage in some banter with each other, with Rodger also adopting the former's tendency to point out minor smudges on glass. One of Glisten's notes in his [[Roleplay]] room also expresses wanting to spend more time with him.
*It was confirmed in the New Year QnA Stream that both {{CI|Vee|name=true}} and Rodger don't have mouths and don't need to eat, but they can eat the in-game food items for gameplay purposes. Nothing related to this was said about the other mouthless Toons.
*Rodger is one of the four [[Toons]] who has a [[Skin]] ({{Skin|Ebony Detective}}) designed by someone else other than the developers, with the others being {{Skin|Dapperly Festive|toon={{CI|Looey|name=true}}}}, {{Skin|Special Spaghetti|toon={{CI|Goob|name=true}}}}, and {{Skin|Choco Cones|toon={{CI|Yatta|name=true}}}}.
*In [[Changelog|v0.9.1]], Rodger was given a buff to where if he would encounter a [[Twisted]] for the first time in the Floor, he would receive 20 {{Tape|name=true}} instead of the usual 5. This was later reverted in v0.9.4.
*Rodger is the first [[Toon]] whose corresponding [[Trinket]] (the {{TI|Magnifying Glass|name=true}}) is the same species as him, the second being {{CI|Coal|name=true}}.
**However, unlike Rodger, Coal's Trinket shares the same color as her body and the same name.
***His Trinket is stowed in his torso when not serving as part of his Passive Ability animation, like how Vee's microphone is stowed in her head when not being used for an idle animation.
*The 8/10/2025 QnA Art Stream revealed Rodger and {{CI|Dyle|name=true}} aren't related. This is further emphasized by Dyle revealing via [[Gossip]] that he isn't allowed to talk to Rodger.
*Rodger is the last [[Toon]] with a teased optimization to actually receive one, with other Toons like [[Vee]], [[Shelly]] and {{CI|Astro|name=true}} getting theirs prior to his in [[Changelog|v0.13.14]].
*Rodger had an old icon pose that resembled {{CI|Boxten|name=true}}'s information card pose. This was probably a placeholder before the developers could start working on it.
*When collecting [[Research]], Rodger will inspect the [[Capsule]] with a small [[Magnifying Glass|magnifying glass]]. This visual quirk was added in his optimization in [[Changelog|v0.13.14]].
**As it can be assumed that this is Rodger's [[Trinket]], this is the fourth instance of a Trinket having its own in-game model, with the first being with {{TI|Blue Bandana|name=true}} for [[Boxten]] and {{TI|Pink Bow|name=true}} for [[Poppy]], the second being with {{TI|Feather Duster|name=true}}, present in {{CI|Tisha|name=true}}'s Active [[Ability]], and the third being with the {{TI|Sweet Charm|name=true}} and the {{TI|Savory Charm|name=true}}, both in the idle animations of {{CI|Cosmo|name=true}} and {{CI|Sprout|name=true}}, respectively.
*Rodger is one of the few [[Toons]] to have their default pose changed following optimization, since he originally had his hands in front of his chest, and now he has them behind his back similar to [[Tisha]].
*The {{Skin|Ebony Detective}} [[Skin]] was redone after his optimization, making it more distinct than just a recolor.
*Sometimes, when spawning/resetting in the lobby, {{Skin|Alpha Sleeper Rodger}} will lose his glass.
**This is the only Rodger [[Skin]] this can happen to.
*Rodger and [[Gigi]] are the fourth [[Toons]] to appear twice in 2 separate thumbnails, being from [[Changelog|v0.11]] and v0.13.14, the first being {{CI|Pebble|name=true}}, the second being {{CI|Shrimpo|name=true}}, the third being [[Toodles]], the fifth being {{CI|Bobette|name=true}}, and the sixth being the rest of the [[Christmas Toons]].
*Rodger's full icon/[[Introduction Card]] actually has design differences compared to his model, with the icon having a vest with a V shaped bottom and the his magnifying glass' handle being smaller with a shorter strap.
*It is highly likely Rodger knows all the [[Main Characters]]' full names, as he refers to them by their last name sometimes. Additionally, in [[Bobette]] and [[Toodles]] interaction, Bobette is aware that Rodger knows her full name.
*Rodger is the second Toon to get a [[Code]] [[Skin]], the first being {{CI|Yatta|name=true}}.
*Rodger appears to be cross dominant. He uses his right hand to hold his magnifying glass and to hold a flashlight in the "Lights Out Investigation" episode poster. Meanwhile, he uses his left hand to carry his briefcase and to extract when his {{Skin|Research-mobile}} is equipped.
*Rodger's {{Skin|Research-mobile}} [[Skin]] is based on a popular joke within the fandom where Rodger has an obsession with [[Research]], and a tendency for players to play as him when a new [[Toon]] or [[Event]] is released. Its main inspiration was also a drawing where Rodger is riding a capsule-shaped mobile.<ref>[[File:Research-mobile Origin.png|200px]]</ref>
*Rodger's {{Skin|Mysterious Spy}} [[Skin]] may be inspired by The Invisible Man, though he lacks the dark glasses of the specific lookalike incarnation.

